720 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E (Look beyond traditional arms control to build the legal basis for accountability for CW use. It is essential that arms control and humanitarian/war crimes communities work collaboratively to maximize national and international prosecutorial pathways.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
721 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E ( Build and support national capacities for enforcing CW norms. National authorities will always be the accountability pathway of first resort. It is vital to make better use of national tools and authorities, especially in coordination and collaboration with law enforcement entities across governments. This must include efforts to raise national technical and forensic capacities for diagnostics and chain of custody. Targeted capacity-building efforts through the Global Partnership, European Union, and U.S.-based cooperative threat reduction programs could pay big dividends.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
